---
import ProductLayout from '../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
---
<ProductLayout title="Support — ExpenseTracking | Facware" description="Get help with ExpenseTracking, local data, exports, and optional Google Drive backup." canonicalURL="https://web-expense-tracking.facware.com/support.html">
  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-container">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Help center</p>
      <h1>ExpenseTracking support</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Product support from Facware</p>
      <p>For help with setup, exports, data recovery, or Google Drive backup, email <a href="mailto:contact@facware.com">contact@facware.com</a>. Please describe your browser, device, application version if known, and the steps that led to the problem. Never send passwords, OAuth tokens, or real financial records.</p>
      <h2>Common data controls</h2>
      <ul><li>Use the app’s JSON, PDF, or CSV export to keep a copy of your records.</li><li>Clear local application data only after confirming you have a usable export.</li><li>Delete Drive backups from Google Drive when you want them removed.</li><li>Revoke ExpenseTracking from your Google Account if you no longer want Drive access.</li></ul>
      <h2>Privacy and deletion requests</h2>
      <p>Send privacy, access, or deletion requests to <a href="mailto:contact@facware.com">contact@facware.com</a>. See the <a href="/privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a> for details about local data, Drive data, retention, and requests.</p>
      <h2>Other links</h2>
      <p><a href="/security.html">Security and vulnerability reporting</a> · <a href="/terms-of-service.html">Terms of Service</a> · <a href="/privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</ProductLayout>
